# Round 1.3.8: TLS handshake crypto bench on boot (CONFIG_TINYLINK_BENCH_TLS,
# components/tinylink/src/tinylink_bench_tls.c lists every line it prints).
# It runs first thing in bringup(), before NVS and Wi-Fi (~1.5-3 s on the
# chip), then the firmware boots normally. One image per configuration:
#
#   idf.py -B <dir> -D SDKCONFIG=<dir>/sdkconfig \
#     -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;tools/tls_bench/sdkconfig.bench[;<A/B>]" build
#
#   <A/B> (none)   the 1.3.8 defaults: RSA first, in-tree X25519, bignum
#                  multiplication in software, RSA exponentiation on the
#                  accelerator
#         sdkconfig.mul-hw   multiplication on the accelerator too (as up to 1.3.7)
#         sdkconfig.mpi-off  no accelerator at all (RSA in software too)
#         sdkconfig.win2 / win3 / win5, sdkconfig.nofp   ECC-only knobs (QEMU
#                  instruction counts settle these; CHANGELOG 1.3.8)
#
# On the chip: flash the app partition, capture the boot (opening the port
# resets the board) and keep the `bench-tls:` lines:
#   python tools/serial_capture.py --port <port> --duration 30 --out <log>
#   grep -a 'bench-tls:' <log>
# On Espressif QEMU add sdkconfig.qemu (DIO flash) and run with
# -icount shift=0: the printed µs are then thousands of instructions; the
# RSA accelerator is emulated with no latency.
CONFIG_TINYLINK_BENCH_TLS=y
